title: D3_15_Closing
---
<<Owen Neutral>>
Owen: And now I'm all alone again.
Player: I told you, you have me.
Owen: That's true.
Owen: What do you think they are to each other?
Player: Faye and Arthur?
Player: How am I supposed to know?
Owen: I suppose so.
Owen: The town is actually quieter than the forest.
Player: That's normal. The louder the sound, the quieter it seems once it stops.
Owen: You're right again.
Owen: Anyway, I have to go now.
Player: Morning shift?
<<Owen Happy>>
Owen: Nope. I'm going to play a game.
Player: ...
<<Owen Neutral>>
Owen: Just kidding. I have to head back into the forest tomorrow.
Owen: I'm going to conduct a survey to see if any bears are wandering close to town.
Player: That sounds serious.
Owen: [fade]It's normal. They're just lost, or... lonely.[/fade]
Owen: See you another day.
Player: Good luck catching the bear.
Owen: [shake]I don't catch them, damn it. I herd them.[/shake]
Player: Haha. Good night.
<<Owen Happy>>
Owen: Night night.
// Owen exits. End of Day 3.
<<Owen Look L>>
<<Owen Exit>>
